the trainer api  the transformers library provides a  trainer api that allows you to easily  fine-tune transformers models  on your data set the trainer class  secure data sets  your model as well as the training ipad  parameters  and can perform the training on any kind  of setup cpu gpu  multiple gpus tpus can also compute the  predictions on any data set and if your  provided metrics  evaluate your model on any data set  you can also undo final data processing  such as dynamic padding  as long as you provide the tokenizer or  a given data collater  we'll try this api in the mrpc dataset  since it's relatively small  and easy to pre-process as we saw in the  datasets overview video  very though we can preprocess it we do  not apply padding during the  preprocessing  as we will use dynamic padding with our  data collector with padding  note that we don't do the final steps of  renaming removing columns  or set the format to torch tensors the  trainer will do all of this  automatically for us  by analyzing the model's signature  the last step before creating the  trainer are to define our model  and some training upper parameters we  see how to do the first  in the model api video for the second  we use the training argument class it  only takes a path to a folder where  results and checkpoint will be saved  but you can also customize all the other  parameters that your trainer will use  learning rate number of training inbox  etc  it's been very easy to create a trainer  on launcher training  this should display a progress bar and  after a few minutes  if you're running on a gpu you should  have the training finished  the result will be rather anticlimactic  however as you will only get a training  loss  which doesn't really tell you anything  about how well your model is performing  this is because we didn't specify any  metric for the evaluation  to get those metrics we'll first cover  the predictions on the wall evaluation  set  using the predict method it returns a  name to paul with three fields  prediction which contains the model  predictions label ids  which contains the labels if you data  set at them and metrics which is empty  here  we're trying to do that the predictions  are the luggage of the models for all  the sentences in the data set  so an empire ray of shape 408 by two  to match them with our labels we need to  take the maximum logic for each  prediction  to know which of the two classes was  predicted we do  this with the rmax function then we can  use the matrix from the datasets library  it can be loaded as easily as a dataset  with the loadmetric function  and it returns the evaluation metric  used for the dataset  we can see our model did learn something  as it is 85.7 percent accurate  to monitor the evaluation matrix during  training we need to define a compute  metric function  that does the same step as before it  takes a name to pull with predictions  and labels  and must return a dictionary of the  metrics we want to keep track of  by passing the epoch evaluation strategy  to our training arguments  we tell the trainer to evaluate at the  end of every epoch  launching a training inside a notebook  will then display a progress bar  and complete the table you see here as  you pass every epoch
 

